<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#creates> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "ISO/IEC 22989, 3.1.27 defines the prediction as the primary output of an AI system when provided with input data."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#basedOnAlgorithm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> _:N0bf1d81377c3457abfa46e8e1713cf21 .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#EvaluationData> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "ISO/IEC 22989, 3.2.14, where the entry carries both names, test data and evaluation data.\n\nNote 1 states that it is disjoint from training data and validation data. The pattern asserts that disjointness, since evaluating a model on data it was trained on says nothing about its performance."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Inference> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "ISO/IEC 22989, 3.1.17. Note 1 to the entry states that in AI a premise is either a fact, a rule, a model, a feature or raw data, which is why both a symbolic and a subsymbolic system perform inference.\n\nNote 2 adds that the term refers both to the process and its result. This pattern uses it for the process and records the result as a prediction, 3.1.27."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Model> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#basedOnLearning> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#LearningType> .
_:N8444fd5a2924438f882b701dc2f1bda4 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#List> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Task> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Task"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Imputation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Imputation"@en .
