<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://www.iso.org/standard/74296.html> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#forCharacteristic> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#VariableCharacteristic> .
_:N6dc6ea904e3b4be39232ce3598b29f3d <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#List> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#AIType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "**Collecting class of this pattern.** The standard defines symbolic AI, 3.1.33, and subsymbolic AI, 3.1.34, and compares them in clause 5.9, but names no common superclass for the two.\n\nThe two kinds are deliberately **not** disjoint. Neither entry excludes the other, and clause 5.9 discusses combining them, so a system may be typed as both."@en .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#isProcessedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates data to a data process step applied to it."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#MachineLearning> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The process of optimizing model parameters through computational techniques, such that the model's behaviour reflects the data or experience."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#DataSource> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "**Construct of this work.** Discussed in ISO/IEC 22989, clause 8.6.1, without an entry. One of the two points at which an AI system meets what surrounds it."@en .
_:Nc7aeeaa8781b4d40aed34d3a09647734 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#List> .
