<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#isEvaluatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#forCharacteristic> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Functional: one value quantifies exactly one characteristic."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Algorithm> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Model> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#MachineLearning> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Machine Learning"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#ProductionData> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Data> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#realisedByModel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The step from the structural element to what makes it work. A component without a model performs functions but decides nothing."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#isStoredBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Data> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#isStoredBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates data to the storing that persisted it."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Label> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespacePrefix> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#AISystem> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "AI System"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Algorithm> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Data> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#MLModel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "ISO/IEC 22989, 3.3.7. 3.3.14 calls the result of training a trained model.\n\nKept below the general model on purpose. Every machine learning model is a model, but a model is not necessarily learned, and a pattern that knew only this class could not record a symbolic system at all."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#hasDesign> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#SupervisedLearning> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Storing> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "**Construct of this work.** Discussed in ISO/IEC 22989, clause 8.6.1, without an entry. The counterpart of acquisition, and the second function reaching outside the system."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Training> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#AIFunction> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#hasDesign> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#AISystem> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#consistsOf> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#AISystem> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#isAcquiredBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is acquired by"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Ontology design pattern for the terminology of artificial intelligence according to ISO/IEC 22989:2022, Information technology, Artificial intelligence, Artificial intelligence concepts and terminology.\n\nThe pattern describes an AI system in three views: what it is made of and what it does, which algorithms and models carry it, and which data it runs on. The standard supplies an internationally agreed vocabulary for all three.\n\nOne distinction runs through the whole pattern. Symbolic AI, 3.1.33, and subsymbolic AI, 3.1.34, both rest on models, but only the second learns them. The pattern therefore keeps the general model, 3.1.23, above the machine learning model, 3.3.7, so that a rule-based system can be recorded without pretending it was trained.\n\nThe pattern is one of four subdomain patterns of the AIAS information model. It is designed to be imported through owl:imports and aligned by way of the AIAS alignment ontology. Named individuals for the qualities are supplied separately in ISO22989-instances.ttl."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#ProductionData> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Data acquired during the operation phase of an AI system, for which a deployed system calculates a predicted output or inference."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#isProcessedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Data> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#AIFunction> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An activity in the life cycle of an AI system, transforming inputs into outputs."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Acquisition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#AIFunction> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#hasFunction> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#AIFunction> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Data> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
_:N7994055d174744b588e29759fc466dfc <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#ValidationData> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "development data"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#hasSetting> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "ISO/IEC 22989, 3.3.4 defines the hyperparameter as selected prior to training. Its value is therefore set rather than measured, and it is reached by a relation of its own rather than through forCharacteristic.\n\nBoth relations end at the same class, and the direction they run in is what keeps them apart. A characteristic value points to the quality it quantifies, and a hyperparameter points to the value it was given. A model can then be asked which of its values were stated and which were established, which is the first question an audit of a training asks.\n\nFunctional: a hyperparameter carries one value. Two runs at different learning rates are two hyperparameter individuals rather than one with two values, since the value belongs to the run and not to the name."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Control> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "ISO/IEC 22989, 3.5.5, which takes the definition from IEC 61800-7-1:2015, 3.2.6.\n\nModelled as a function alongside training, inference and the rest. The entry sits in clause 3.5 among the terms related to trustworthiness, but that is a grouping by subject rather than a statement about the kind of term: the definition says action, which is what the other functions are as well. A system therefore relates to it through hasFunction like any other activity.\n\n**The wording is identical to IEC 60050-351, 351-42-19**, and both trace back to the same source. The two are the same concept rather than merely similar ones, and the alignment relates them with owl:equivalentClass. This pattern states nothing about the other, since referencing another namespace would drag it along wherever this pattern is used."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#isComposedOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "ISO/IEC 22989, 3.2.5 and 3.2.13. One relation for both levels, since the standard describes a grouping in each case."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#ProductionData> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Evaluation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
_:N4335b96981714d2d81b054f2d0f6e21c <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:N6dc6ea904e3b4be39232ce3598b29f3d .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Algorithm> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "**Construct of this work.** ISO/IEC 22989 defines the machine learning algorithm, 3.3.6, but no general algorithm and no superclass for the kinds below.\n\nThe class exists so that the hyperparameter, 3.3.4, has one place to attach to. The standard defines the hyperparameter for the machine learning algorithm, whereas a model algorithm and an evaluation algorithm carry one as well, for example the number of layers of a network or the threshold of a metric."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Prediction> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "ISO/IEC 22989, 3.1.27.\n\nNote 2 to the entry states that prediction does not necessarily refer to predicting something in the future, and note 1 that predictions can be followed by further outputs such as recommendations, decisions and actions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#SymbolicAI> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "AI based on techniques and models that manipulate symbols and structures according to explicitly defined rules to obtain inferences."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Storing> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#realisedByModel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Model> .
_:N0ead21085d594d6d81a227d77d121c9e <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#List> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#usesData> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#AIFunction> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Label> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "ISO/IEC 22989, 3.2.10. Whether data carries labels is what 3.3.12 and 3.3.17 turn on."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#fulfilsTask> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#hasFunction> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#consistsOfStep> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#DataProcess> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#realisedByModel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#AIComponent> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#AISystem> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#VariableCharacteristic> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#basedOnAlgorithm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "based on algorithm"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#DataSink> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Where data is stored, for example a database or a cloud service."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Prediction> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Prediction"@en .
