<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#hasParameter> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "ISO/IEC 22989, 3.3.8. Only a learned model has these, which is why a symbolic model carries hyperparameters instead.\n\nThe name leads to the model parameter, 3.3.8, and not to the hyperparameter, 3.3.4. The two entries are close enough in wording that the distinction is worth stating: this one is determined by a training, the other is chosen before it."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#ValidationData> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "ISO/IEC 22989, 3.2.15. Note 1 to the entry states that validation data is disjoint from test data and generally also from training data."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#ProductionData> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Production Data"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#consistsOfStep> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates a data processing function to the steps it is made of."@en .
