<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Clustering> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A task identifying groups of similar samples."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Prediction> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Controllability> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "ISO/IEC 22989, 3.5.6.\n\nModelled as a class rather than as a named quality because a model states what the intervention consists of, not a number. It is the entry that matters most for an AI system inside an automated plant."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#LearningType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Learning Type"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#isCreatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Training> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "model training"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#usesMetric> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#fulfilsTask> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "What closes the circle from the output back to the objective the system was built for, 3.1.4.\n\nFunctional: one prediction addresses one task. A prediction serving two purposes is two predictions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#MLAlgorithm> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "ISO/IEC 22989, 3.3.6. The only algorithm the standard defines. What kind of learning it performs is recorded through basedOnLearning."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Acquisition> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#AIType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "AI Type"@en .
