<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Hyperparameter> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "ISO/IEC 22989, 3.3.4, which defines it as a characteristic of a machine learning algorithm affecting its learning process, selected prior to training.\n\nThis pattern places it on the algorithm superclass, so that a model algorithm and an evaluation algorithm may carry one as well: the number of layers of a network, or the threshold of a rule. Applying the entry beyond machine learning is a reading of it rather than the entry itself, and a rule threshold recorded here is such a case.\n\nThe value chosen for it is reached by hasSetting, not by forCharacteristic. A hyperparameter is set before a training and a quality of clause 3.5 is established by one, and the two relations keep that difference readable."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Sample> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Sample"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#unit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#CharacteristicValue> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Data> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "**Collecting class of this pattern.** The standard defines the dataset, 3.2.5, and the sample, 3.2.13, and grades data by its use, but names no class between the atom and the collection."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#ValidationData> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Validation Data"@en .
