<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#ModelAlgorithm> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "**Construct of this work**, derived from ISO/IEC 22989, 3.1.23 and 3.3.7.\n\nIt is what a model is before its parameters are known. The distinction matters because the same architecture trained on different data yields different models, and a model records which of the two it is talking about.\n\nA concrete architecture is recorded as a named individual of this class rather than as a subclass, which keeps the pattern independent of libraries and methods."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Training> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The process to determine or to improve the parameters of a machine learning model, based on a machine learning algorithm, by using training data."@en .
