<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#hasFunction> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The step from what a system is to what it does. Where a system has components, the functions are related to those rather than to the system, so that two components performing the same kind of function stay apart."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#hasDesign> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#SystemDesign> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Hybrid> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The combination of the two above. A system whose components run in different places is recorded this way."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#SubsymbolicAI> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "AI based on techniques and models that use an implicit encoding of information, that can be derived from experience or raw data."@en .
