<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#basedOnLearning> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates a machine learning algorithm to the kind of learning it performs."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#MLAlgorithm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An algorithm to determine parameters of a machine learning model from data according to given criteria."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Sampling> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Training> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "ISO/IEC 22989, 3.3.15.\n\nThe entry names all three ingredients: an algorithm, training data and the parameters that come out. A training missing any of them is not one, which is what makes this function the place where the difference between an algorithm and a model arises."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Augmentation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#DataProcess> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Algorithm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Algorithm"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#DataSource> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Where data is acquired from, for example a sensor or a database."@en .
