<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#DataProcess> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Data Process"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#isValidatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Model> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#AISystem> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An engineered system that generates outputs such as content, forecasts, recommendations or decisions for a given set of human-defined objectives."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Generation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Generation"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#ModelAlgorithm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The procedure describing the structure of a model, such as the architecture of a neural network or a set of rules."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#SystemDesign> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "**Construct of this work.** Clause 8.6.2 of the standard discusses cloud and edge computing without defining the choice between them as a term.\n\nThe class is kept because it is what connects an AI system to the plant it runs in: the design says which device carries which part of the system, which is the handover the alignment needs."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Normative basis: ISO/IEC 22989:2022.\n\nClause 3 of the standard holds 115 entries and this pattern takes up 47 of them. REFERENCE.md lists every entry with the reason it is taken or left out, so the selection is checkable rather than asserted. Three whole clauses stay out: neural networks, natural language processing and computer vision name techniques and application fields, both open sets. A model using a convolutional network records it as a named individual of the model algorithm class instead.\n\nSome classes here have no entry in clause 3. Five of them are collecting classes the standard needs but does not name, such as the common superclass of the four kinds of learning. The rest are constructs of this work. Every one of them says so on its own skos:note, and REFERENCE.md lists them apart from the entries.\n\nNo class of another namespace appears in this pattern. Where a term matches a term of another standard, as control, 3.5.5, matches IEC 60050-351, 351-42-19, word for word, the two are related in the alignment ontology rather than here. A pattern that referenced another would drag it along wherever it is used."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#hasControllability> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has controllability"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Hyperparameter> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#SubsymbolicAI> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Subsymbolic AI"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#hasFunction> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> _:N69593c7c023147e9be04906109c05d8b .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#quantity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The numeric quantity of a characteristic value."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Regression> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A task predicting continuous quantities."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Cloud> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#SystemDesign> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#ProductionData> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "ISO/IEC 22989, 3.2.12.\n\nNot part of the disjointness above. It arises during operation, so it cannot overlap with data that existed before deployment."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#SemiSupervisedLearning> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "ISO/IEC 22989, 3.3.11."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#usesData> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Which kind of data belongs to which function follows from the entries: 3.3.16 for training, 3.2.15 for validation, 3.2.14 for evaluation and 3.2.12 for inference in operation."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#isAcquiredBy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "What makes the origin of data traceable. Data without one is data a model cannot account for."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Sample> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "ISO/IEC 22989, 3.2.13."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#Acquisition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Acquisition"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#ValidationData> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#isValidatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is validated by"@en .
